# Three.js Birthday Cake Project

Browser-based Three.js scene of a cozy retro birthday cake built from real 3D cylindrical geometry.

Files:
- `index.html`: Browser entry point and Three.js import map.
- `styles/style.css`: Full-screen responsive canvas and retro pixelated rendering style.
- `src/main.js`: App bootstrap.
- `src/scene.js`: Renderer, camera, lighting, shadows, plate, floor, and responsive sizing.
- `src/cake.js`: Layered cylindrical cake geometry, lavender frosting, drips, icing, candle, flame, and decorations.
- `src/animations.js`: Infinite cakeGroup rotation, local candle sway, flame flicker, and sparkles.
- `src/animation.js`: Compatibility re-export for older imports.
- `src/ui.js`: Action-I "Click Me!" chase sequence and birthday reveal placeholder.
- `server.mjs`: Tiny local static server using Node built-ins.
- `package.json`: `npm install` and `npm run dev` workflow.
- `scripts/vendor-three.mjs`: Copies Three.js from `node_modules` into `vendor`.
- `vendor/three/build/three.module.js`: Local Three.js module used by the browser import map.

Install and run:

```powershell
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open `http://localhost:5173`.

You can also run the static server directly:

```powershell
node server.mjs
```
